Thanks for taking on #27. The current diff only adds a 16-byte placeholder file containing `/* new code */`, so it does not yet implement or verify the requested subtitle fixtures.

Please update the PR with the actual acceptance deliverables:

- one synthetic, copyright-clean clip and subtitle fixture for each of 16:9, 9:16, and 1:1;
- a checked-in generator or documented FFmpeg command;
- long Chinese and English lines, punctuation, two speakers, and a high-detail lower-third region;
- D4 verifier evidence for at most two lines, safe margins, readable font size, no clipping, and no occlusion;
- native-resolution review screenshots;
- a green `pnpm check` receipt.

Please keep the existing default subtitle style and injection escaping unchanged. Once there is an executable fixture set and evidence, we can review the implementation rather than the placeholder.
